{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4809-1","published":"2026-10-21T08:04:20Z","modified":"2026-10-21T20:02:16.071878701Z","related":["CVE-2026-15310","CVE-2026-15806","CVE-2026-17084","CVE-2026-19445","CVE-2026-19553","CVE-2026-19672","CVE-2026-82049"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-15310","CVE-2026-15806","CVE-2026-17084","CVE-2026-19445","CVE-2026-19553","CVE-2026-19672","CVE-2026-82049"],"summary":"Security update for python311","details":"This update for python311 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-15310: memory exhaustion in zipfile in bzip2/LZMA/Zstandard decompression (bsc#1277111).\n- CVE-2026-15806: urllib.request.HTTPPasswordMgr credentials for one URL scheme sent over another scheme (bsc#1276223).\n- CVE-2026-17084: StringPrep algorithm considered Unicode codepoint attributes outside Unicode 3.2.0 (bsc#1276226).\n- CVE-2026-19445: reassigned SNI callbacks with unreferenced SSLContext instances can cause use-after-free\n  (bsc#1283969).\n- CVE-2026-19553: omitted server_hostname arguments in wrap_bio() can cause silent hostname verification bypasses\n  (bsc#1283826).\n- CVE-2026-19672: tarfile extraction filter bypass allows creation of directories outside the destination (bsc#1276227).\n- CVE-2026-82049: tarfile extraction filters mishandle archives containing a hard link to a symbolic link, allowing file\n  modification and content disclosure (bsc#1280459).\n\nChanges for python311:\n\n- Update to 3.11.17:\n - Library\n - gh-156002: zipfile again reads members through a\n third-party decompressor installed by monkey-patching the\n private _get_decompressor() to return an object that only\n implements old BZ2Decompressor API from Python 3.3. Note\n that decompressors without needs_input and two-argument\n decompress() are vulnerable to CVE 2026-15310.\n - gh-156353: Fix configparser parsing when using whitespace\n in delimiters.\n - Build\n - gh-155757: Set the --argv0 argument to wasmtime for WASI\n builds so the test suite passes. Otherwise the calculated\n paths to the stdlib for frozen modules is incorrect.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python311","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Public Cloud 15 SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python311&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Public%20Cloud%2015%20SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_11-1_0":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-base":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4809-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python311-core","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Public Cloud 15 SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python311-core&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Public%20Cloud%2015%20SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_11-1_0":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-base":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4809-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python311","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python311&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libpython3_11-1_0":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-base":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-curses":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-dbm":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-devel":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-doc":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-doc-devhelp":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-idle":"3.11.17-150400.9.105.1","python311-tk":"3.11.17-15